A||||4||kempo||Cant Shift into Gear||||1||
Z||000000||kempo||09-16-2001||10:10 PM||||Was driving it just fine last night with no problems.  Today I got out and started her up, and she wouldn't go into any gear, and if forced, would grind.  Turn her off, and she'd shift into 2,3,4,5 but not 1 and reverse.  Rolled her up into the garage and bled the clutch for air, got a lot of air out, but still didn't help solve the problem.  I am thinking that my clutch isn't engaging all the way?  Perhaps my hydrualics are shot?  Or my slave cylinder is all gummed up and needs cleaning/rebuilding?  I don't know where to go from here, so I thought I'd check with the experts (aka- you guys) before I attempt anything.  This really sucks because I can't drive her anywhere.  <P>87 GT / 5 Speed Getrag &lt;--- being a b*tch!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.admist.net/kempsig.jpg"> <BR>87 Fiero GT / 5 Speed<BR>86 Fiero 2m4 - FOR SALE||||reg||1
Z||000001||SLYGUY||09-17-2001||02:00 AM||||My 88 GT was shifting hard. Pulled out the speed sensor to check the fluid level (turned out there was a dipstick that Haynes didn't know about) and it was black, AND low.<P>Changed the fluid, and it is much better now.<P>Try that, and check your fluid level in the clutch cylinder.<P>Sly<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SLYGUYSIG.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||kempo||09-17-2001||11:54 AM||||Is yours an Automatic?  I can't seem to find the dipstick you speak of, could you tell me the location of it?  The clutch fluid level is full and the system is bled.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Indiana_resto_guy||09-17-2001||12:05 PM||||If you locate your speed sensor, look to the left on the other side of the case.<BR>IF yours is a Getrag (by Muncie), there will be a small dip stick that you unscrew with a flat tab that sticks up.||||reg||1
Z||000004||SLYGUY||09-17-2001||12:12 PM||||Mine is a 5 spd. <P>Indiana is right. Like I said, Haynes manuals describe pulling the speed sensor out to check the fluid lever. I saw a dipstick labeled "Trans Fill" about two inches towards the left rear tire from the speed sensor. Used that to check fluid level/fill the tranny.<P>Sly<P>P.S. I used baby oil when I refilled it. Is this gonna hurt anything. Just kiddin'<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SLYGUYSIG.jpg"> ||||reg||1
